{"name":"Rojo Oxide","hex":"#8d4942","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"oxide","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A binary chemical compound of oxygen with another chemical element."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oxide"}],"entries":[{"title":"Oxide","blocks":[{"text":"An oxide is a chemical compound containing at least one oxygen atom and one other element in its chemical formula. \"Oxide\" itself is the dianion of oxygen, an O2− ion with oxygen in the oxidation state of −2. Most of the Earth's crust consists of oxides. Even materials considered pure elements often develop an oxide coating. For example, aluminium foil develops a thin skin of Al2O3 that protects the foil from further oxidation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Rutile-unit-cell-3D-balls.png/330px-Rutile-unit-cell-3D-balls.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oxide","wikidata":"Q50690"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Nitrous-oxide-2D-dimensions.png/250px-Nitrous-oxide-2D-dimensions.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Nitrous-oxide-2D-dimensions.png/330px-Nitrous-oxide-2D-dimensions.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Nitrous-oxide-2D-dimensions.png/250px-Nitrous-oxide-2D-dimensions.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANitrous-oxide-2D-dimensions.png"}],"sounds":{"oxide":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/26/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-oxide.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedi